b.com/users/raulsntos","html_url":"https://github.com/raulsntos","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-24T17:42:51Z","updated_at":"2026-09-24T17:42:51Z","body":"You are creating new instances on the `_RenderCallback` method, which is called often. C# instances are not collected immediately by the GC, only when a threshold is reached. You can see that this is not a memory leak by using `GC.Collect()`, which forces the GC to collect C# instances that are no longer referenced, but it's not recommended to use `GC.Collect()` in production, let the GC work as intended and collect when it deems it necessary.\n\nAs for `NotificationPredelete`, C# scripts won't receive it because the instance is disposed first. If you need to cleanup, override the [`Dispose`](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/standard/garbage-collection/implementing-dispose) method.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5819141178/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5990148408","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/121460#issuecomment-5